---@class aws.marketplace_agreement.DescribeAgreementInput
---@field agreementId aws.marketplace_agreement.ResourceId The unique identifier of the agreement.

---@class aws.marketplace_agreement.DescribeAgreementOutput
---@field agreementId? aws.marketplace_agreement.ResourceId The unique identifier of the agreement.
---@field acceptor? aws.marketplace_agreement.Acceptor The details of the party accepting the agreement terms. This is commonly the buyer for PurchaseAgreement.
---@field proposer? aws.marketplace_agreement.Proposer The details of the party proposing the agreement terms. This is commonly the seller for PurchaseAgreement.
---@field startTime? aws.marketplace_agreement.Timestamp The date and time when the agreement starts.
---@field endTime? aws.marketplace_agreement.Timestamp The date and time when the agreement ends. The field is null for pay-as-you-go agreements, which don’t have end dates.
---@field acceptanceTime? aws.marketplace_agreement.Timestamp The date and time the offer was accepted or the agreement was created.
---@field agreementType? aws.marketplace_agreement.AgreementType The type of agreement. Values are PurchaseAgreement or VendorInsightsAgreement.
---@field estimatedCharges? aws.marketplace_agreement.EstimatedCharges The estimated cost of the agreement.
---@field proposalSummary? aws.marketplace_agreement.ProposalSummary A summary of the proposal received from the proposer.
---@field status? aws.marketplace_agreement.AgreementStatus The current status of the agreement.
---@field initialAgreementId? aws.marketplace_agreement.ResourceId The unique identifier of the very first agreement in a chain of related agreements, such as renewals or replacements. It stays the same across all agreements in that chain, which lets you trace an agreement back to the original. When an agreement isn't derived from another agreement, its InitialAgreementId is its own AgreementId.
---@field endTimeBehavior? aws.marketplace_agreement.EndTimeBehavior The behavior of the agreement when it reaches its end date. For example, whether the agreement renews, and if it doesn't, the reason why.
---@field freeTrialSummary? aws.marketplace_agreement.FreeTrialSummary The free trial details of the agreement. This field is present only when the agreement includes a free trial.

